---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
---

<Page
  title="About WorldTripMap"
  description="WorldTripMap is a free tool for mapping where you have been and turning it into a poster. What it does, the principles behind it, and how to reach us."
  h1="About WorldTripMap"
  lede="WorldTripMap is a free tool for keeping track of where you have been, and for turning that record into something you would hang on a wall."
  crumb="About"
  path="/about/"
>
  <h2>What it is</h2>
  <p>
    You mark the countries, provinces or cities you have explored. The site counts them, shows your progress, and draws a poster from
    them that you can download as a picture or a print-ready PDF. It launched with the world, Canada’s provinces and territories, and
    Canadian cities. More countries will follow one at a time, each published only when its map is accurate and complete.
  </p>

  <h2>What we care about</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Real maps.</strong> Every place is a real geographic shape from a named, openly licensed dataset, drawn in a projection chosen
      for that map. Nothing on the site is a decorative picture pretending to be interactive.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Numbers that say what they mean.</strong> A percentage is always a share of the places on the map, and the page says so
      beside it. The <a href="/methodology/">data and methods page</a> sets out every rule.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your travels are yours.</strong> There is no account. Your map lives in your own browser, and share links carry the map
      inside the link instead of on our servers. <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a>
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>It should work for everyone.</strong> The maps can be used with a mouse, a finger, a keyboard or a screen reader, and every
      place can also be marked from a plain list.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>No invented praise.</strong> You will not find testimonials, user counts or star ratings here that we cannot back up.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How the guides are written</h2>
  <p>
    The pieces under <a href="/guides/">Travel inspiration</a> are written for this site and checked against primary sources where they
    exist, such as Statistics Canada and the United Nations. Each guide lists its sources and the date they were checked. Guides are
    published under the WorldTripMap name. When we get something wrong, we correct the page and change its “updated” date.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions, corrections and ideas for the next map are welcome at <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a> or
    through the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</Page>
